    "gsap": {
      "repository": "greensock/GSAP",
      "revisions": [],
      "reason": "Neither the published packages nor the upstream repository carry license text: gsap and @gsap/react declare the terms only by URL. The bundled text is the complete \"Standard No Charge GSAP License\" from the official licensing page that both packages name, converted from the page HTML without rewording. The title's \"no charge\" is the license's own name, not a condition; the grant covers commercial and non-commercial use for the defined Permitted Uses, and the substantive restriction is the defined \"Prohibited Uses\" concerning no-code tools that compete with Webflow's visual animation-building capabilities. GSAP's terms are not an SPDX license, are not MIT or Apache-2.0, and are not represented as open source; no compatibility conclusion is drawn here.",
